  "content": "## Accounts, domains and records\n\nResolve account and zone ids before acting. A zone is a domain, found by its name;\nits account id joins it to the account inventory. Cloudflare ids are normally\n32-character hex strings. A default id routes a request; a pin limits its scope.\n\nDNS TTL is in seconds; TTL 1 means automatic. Read the record before changing it.\nPATCH changes supplied fields; PUT replaces the record, so preserve its type,\nname and content. Read state before replacing, rolling back or purging. Prefer\na targeted cache purge by files, tags, hosts or prefixes over purging everything.\n\nHatch data keeps Cloudflare's vendor envelope. For example, select DNS record\nidentities with `fields: [\"result.id\", \"result.name\"]`; a list stays under\n`data.result`. Named account and zone lists keep projected rows with camelCase\naccount and name-server fields.\n\n## Workers, storage and analytics\n\nWorker script source is code; secret binding values are separate and unavailable.\nKV values are application data. Encode a slash inside a KV key or R2 object key\nas `%2F`. R2 requires API-token authentication, rather than a Global API Key.\n\nGraphQL Analytics uses accountTag and zoneTag for account/zone identities.\nFilter every accounts/zones field by equality or an explicit set of those ids.\nA pinned query uses one operation per document and every declared fragment.\nAnalytics Engine SQL is read-only; D1 SQL and Durable Object queries can write.\nAI inference, previews and outbound checks can cost money or activate work.\n\n## Disqualifiers and recovery\n\nCredential minting, rotation, stored secrets, private session captures and signed\nupload or deployment links are unavailable. Use the Cloudflare dashboard for\ncredential administration. A Global API Key cannot change user settings or\nmemberships through this connection.\n\nAfter an authentication failure, use `verify_credential` once to distinguish a\nrejected credential from a permission gap. An operator replaces the credential;\nrepeating the failed request does not add permissions. Cloudflare's global limit\ncounts dashboard traffic and all tokens together, so reduce requests as well as\nhonoring the returned wait.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** while `page.hasMore` is true, continue with `page.nextCursor` unchanged. For `cloudflare_api_details`, `cloudflare_api_search`, `list_accounts`, `list_zones`, pass it as the top-level `cursor`; omit raw paging anchors on continuations. For `cloudflare_api_read`, put it in `query[page.param]` or `body[page.param]`, as `page.in` specifies. Keep the original method, path, filters, page size, fields and headers. Paged `list_*` and `search_*` reads take `limit` (default 20, at most 50). The last page has no `nextCursor`. If `page.hasMore` is true without a cursor, the data is incomplete and continuation was withheld. When approaching execute_code's per-program call limit, return page.nextCursor before the call that would exceed it and continue in the next program; don't restart.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Envelope fields:** hatch data keeps the vendor envelope. Select declared fields with `fields: [\"result.id\", \"result.name\"]`; array traversal also accepts `result[].id`. Named reads keep their projected fields.\n- **Hatch:** `cloudflare_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `cloudflare_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `cloudflare_api_read` calls a reviewed read. Details' `response.fields` promises selection only; `withheld` hints are incomplete, and absence never means safe or readable. `cloudflare_api_write` calls a reviewed write; the host may ask the user to confirm it. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused. 70 operations are refused by design; use `cloudflare_api_details` with the method and path to see each summary and refusal, even for methods outside the read/write schemas.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. Writes take no idempotency key.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. `not_found` means the record does not exist; this API tells absence from a permission gap. It documents no conflict.\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.",
